     "type": "text",
     "text": "{\"count\":0,\"rationale\":\"No single non-foothold step is a chokepoint. Every intermediate step is reachable from the footholds, and the target is an OR over dbReplica, vaultRead, codeRepo and mailArchive. Two routes to the target share no intermediate step. Route A is fileServer to codeRepo to target, where fileServer is an OR of dbLogin and tokenCache, and tokenCache has entry parents supplychain and wifiGuest. Route B is apiToken plus rdpLogin to domainAdmin to mailArchive to target. Because these routes are disjoint, blocking any one step leaves at least one route intact. For example, blocking rdpLogin removes domainAdmin and secretsManager, but fileServer to codeRepo still works. Blocking fileServer leaves domainAdmin to mailArchive and dbReplica.\"}"
    }
   ],
